// test.claim.host.network_install_witness — the witnesses PXE 2c's plan item asks for.
//
// Four of them are named by the plan, and each is driven by a DISCRIMINATING RED plus a REAL-INPUT POSITIVE
// CONTROL, per the plan's own rule ("every witness names the change that would flip it"). The four are:
//   no edge binding means no PATCH              → w_no_edge_binding_plans_no_boot_step, with its red's twin
//   an unread or stale disk reading withholds   → w_the_stale_reading_withholds_the_install_at_its_own_deadline
//   a seed whose match names no single disk     → w_a_model_only_reading_names_no_disk_to_erase
//   a repeat dispatch refuses                   → w_a_completed_install_refuses_the_second_dispatch
// plus the ordering, journal-decoding, contents, hold, completion and settle claims that make those four mean
// what they claim rather than merely pass.
//
// WHAT A WITNESS MAY NOT DEPEND ON. srv15's arrival population row and standing grant land on another branch
// (PXE 1d-a), so no claim here reads the COMMITTED arrival population: every membership claim drives the
// supplied-population form, which is the shape admit_arrival_subject_in was made public for. A claim that said
// "the committed population refuses srv15" would be a claim about a date, and would flip under this file when
// 1d-a lands. The BMC standings are the committed mtcollins1 rows (a real input, not a fixture), because
// BmcSecureStanding is minted only by its own admission and no fixture of it belongs in this file.
module test.claim.host.network_install_witness

